{#- The re-raised failure of tasks/maintain_cycle.yml's block (maintain-nodes),
    in the style of cycle_failed.j2. Says whether the node is held, whether its
    containers run, and what to do. `cs-agent maintenance off` is suggested
    only while no container has been stopped. -#}
{%- set task = ansible_failed_task.name | default('') -%}
{%- set res = ansible_failed_result | default({}) -%}
{%- set why = res.msg | default('') | string -%}
{%- if res.results is defined -%}
{%- set why = why ~ ' ' ~ (res.results | selectattr('failed', 'defined') | selectattr('failed') | map(attribute='msg') | select('defined') | unique | join('; ')) -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if res.stderr | default('') -%}
{%- set why = why ~ ' -- ' ~ (res.stderr | string | trim)[-600:] -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- set backup = cs_site_backup_hosts.get(cs_site, '') if cs_site_backup_hosts is defined else '' -%}
{%- set rerun = 'make maintain-nodes ENV=<env> LIMIT=' ~ inventory_hostname ~ ':' ~ (groups['controller'] | first)
                ~ ((':' ~ backup) if backup else '') -%}
{%- set phases = node_upgrade_phases_done | default([]) -%}
{#- apt refuses every install while an earlier apt/dpkg run is left half-way;
    not repaired automatically (tasks/os_upgrade.yml says why). -#}
{%- set dpkg_broken = (why is search('dpkg --configure -a')) or (why is search('dpkg was interrupted')) -%}
{%- set dpkg_hint = (' DPKG WAS INTERRUPTED (an earlier apt or dpkg run died part-way), so apt refuses every install until it is repaired. On the node, `dpkg --audit` lists the half-configured packages; '
    ~ ('configuring a docker package (' ~ (docker_apt_packages | map('regex_replace', '=.*$', '') | join(', ')) ~ ') restarts dockerd, so if one is listed do it only with the tenant containers stopped; otherwise ' if ('stopped' not in phases or 'started' in phases) else '')
    ~ 'run `dpkg --configure -a`, then re-run.') if dpkg_broken else '' -%}
{%- if node_upgrade_rescue_released | default(false) | bool -%}
"{{ task }}" failed on {{ inventory_hostname }}: {{ why }}
The maintenance hold this run placed has been RELEASED automatically: it failed before the
converge started, so nothing on the node was changed and no container was stopped. Its state
was set aside as state.aborted.*.json in {{ node_upgrade_state_dir }}. Fix the cause, then re-run.
{%- elif node_upgrade_rescue_release | default(false) | bool -%}
"{{ task }}" failed on {{ inventory_hostname }}: {{ why }}
Nothing on the node was changed and no container was stopped, but releasing the hold
automatically failed ({{ (node_upgrade_rescue_off.stdout | default('') | node_upgrade_cli_json).doc.error
| default(node_upgrade_rescue_off.stderr | default('') | trim, true) }}). The node IS HELD.
Re-run `{{ rerun }}` (it resumes inside the hold), or clear it by hand with
`cs-agent maintenance off` and move {{ node_upgrade_state_file }} aside.
{%- elif task is search('Gate - ') -%}
Stopped at "{{ task }}" on {{ inventory_hostname }}; its message above says what state the node is in and what to do.
{%- if node_upgrade_rescue_state.stat.exists %} To resume: `{{ rerun }}`.{% endif %}
{%- elif not node_upgrade_rescue_state.stat.exists -%}
"{{ task }}" failed on {{ inventory_hostname }}: {{ why }}
No maintenance state was written, so this run changed nothing on the node and stopped no
container, and its hold (if `on` placed one) is NOT released automatically: a re-run refuses
while it is there. Run `cs-agent maintenance status` and `docker ps` on the node: if it shows a
local hold with reason `{{ node_upgrade_reason }}` that this run placed, clear it with
`cs-agent maintenance off` (safe: nothing was stopped or changed). Fix the cause, then re-run.
{%- elif node_upgrade_state.releasing | default(false) -%}
"{{ task }}" failed on {{ inventory_hostname }}: {{ why }}
The node had already been RELEASED (`cs-agent maintenance off` ran). Re-run `{{ rerun }}`:
it resumes at the release confirmation, archives {{ node_upgrade_state_file }} and moves on.
{%- elif 'recorded' not in phases -%}
"{{ task }}" failed on {{ inventory_hostname }}: {{ why }}
NODE STATE: {{ inventory_hostname }} IS HELD in maintenance and its tenant containers are
RUNNING -- nothing was stopped. {% if 'converged' in phases %}The converge finished (decision:
{{ 'stop' if (node_upgrade_state.decision.stop | default(false)) else 'no stop' }}).{% else %}The
converge started and may have changed the node's configuration, and applied some of its OS
updates, part-way; a dockerd restart or reboot it needs, if any, has not happened yet.{% endif %}{{ dpkg_hint }}
Fix the cause, then re-run `{{ rerun }}`: it resumes inside the same hold
({{ 'and converges again' if 'converged' not in phases else 'from the recorded decision' }}).
To abandon instead: `cs-agent maintenance off` on the node is safe for the tenants (nothing was
stopped); then move {{ node_upgrade_state_file }} aside. A deferred docker restart is detected
again by the next run (a docker_tls file newer than the running dockerd).
{%- else -%}
"{{ task }}" failed on {{ inventory_hostname }}: {{ why }}
NODE STATE: {{ inventory_hostname }} IS HELD in maintenance, part-way through its stopped
window (phases done: {{ phases | join(', ') }}; state {{ node_upgrade_state_file }}).{{ dpkg_hint }}
{% if 'started' in phases %}The containers recorded there have been started again.
{% elif 'stopped' in phases %}The containers recorded there ARE STOPPED, and nothing
will start them until this playbook does.
{% else %}Some of the containers recorded there may already be stopped.
{% endif %}
Fix the cause, then re-run `{{ rerun }}`: it resumes from the last completed phase. Do NOT
clear the hold with `cs-agent maintenance off` -- the controller would start recovering the
node mid-window, and marks a container inactive after three failed starts in an hour.
{%- endif -%}
